<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  GIZKA_TRIBBLE_ADAPTATION_1 — Card 3, RULED 2026-09-12: "cull guilt: IN."

  Vanilla already charges for killing a BONDED animal and for witnessing a
  slaughter, but most of a gizka swarm is neither bonded nor watched — the
  swarm is exactly the case vanilla's pricing misses, and an unpriced cull
  makes the knife strictly better than every other exit. This is the small
  extra charge that keeps the humane exits competitive: a mood memory, given
  by our own code to any colonist who could SEE a gizka die, stacking so a
  mass cull costs more than a single killing.

  It is deliberately small per head and deliberately stackable. One dead
  gizka is a shrug; forty in an afternoon is a bad week.

  Not a social thought (no "you killed my friend" relationship damage) —
  Thought_Memory, mood only. The bonded case is already vanilla's.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RSW_GizkaWatchedCull</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Memory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>3</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>8</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.85</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>watched the gizka cull</label>
        <description>They were not doing anything. They were just there, and then they were not.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
